From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 07:59:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] RISC OS: path-finding on the main thread

A Pi reported "abort on instruction fetch at &00BB04EC" from another task
(Organizer) during a campaign game. That address is UnixLib's
pthread_call_every, the OS_CallEvery handler that switches threads every
2cs. It lives in our application space and only runs safely while we are
paged in; UnixLib relies on Wimp filters to stop it whenever we call
Wimp_Poll, and it still fired while another task was paged in.

The ticker only runs while a second thread exists, and during a game the
only one is the path-finding thread. UnixLib's threads all share one
core, so that thread bought nothing: it added a context switch every 2cs,
and its idle SDL_Delay(100) busy-waits (SDL only sleeps through the Wimp
on the main thread). On RISC OS the jobs are now run by fpathUpdate() on
the main thread, once per game loop, through the same queue and results
list; the thread code is unchanged, behind FPATH_THREAD, for other
platforms (and for RISC OS, should its threads ever run on other cores).

Checked on Linux with FPATH_THREAD forced to 0: the path-finding
self-test (--selftest, astarTest on two maps, 100 queued paths, with
asserts on) passes, and CAM_1A runs at the same frame rate.
